From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] omcproxy: invalidate cached routes for a changed group

A membership or source-filter change updates downstream group state, but
previously cached upstream source routes still contain the old output set.
Expire only that group's cached sources after updating the client, using
the upstream MRIB and its native exact-group flush operation. Unrelated
groups and multicast interface ownership remain unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>

--- a/src/proxy.c
+++ b/src/proxy.c
@@ -92,8 +92,12 @@ static void proxy_trigger(struct querier
 		bool include, const struct in6_addr *sources, size_t len)
 {
 	struct proxy_downlink *iface = container_of(user, struct proxy_downlink, iface);
-	if (proxy_match_scope(iface->flags, group))
+	struct proxy *proxy = container_of(user->user.querier, struct proxy, querier);
+	if (proxy_match_scope(iface->flags, group)) {
 		client_set(&iface->client, group, include, sources, len);
+		/* Recompute this group's cached sources against the updated downlinks. */
+		mrib_flush(&proxy->mrib, group, 128, NULL);
+	}
 }
 
 // Remove proxy with given name
